System & Network Security Implementation Concepts Lab (CompTIA CySA+)

## Project Overview
     Completed a hands-on cybersecurity lab focused on implementing core system and network security controls in a Windows enterprise environment. The lab emphasized security monitoring, data protection, and identity security through practical configuration and administration tasks. Information derived from Print content.


## Learning Outcomes

In this module, you will complete the following exercises:
    - Exercise 1 - Log Collection with Splunk
    - Exercise 2 - Encrypting Sensitive Data
    - Exercise 3 - Enable Multifactor Authentication

After completing these modules, you should be able to:

    - Install and Configure the Splunk Enterprise Application
    - Configure a Splunk Client
    - Collect Logs using Splunk Enterprise
    - Install the BitLocker Drive Encryption Feature
    - Encrypt a Local Drive on a Server
    - Enable Multifactor Authentication
    - Verify Multifactor Authentication

## Lab Topology

    - ACIDC01 - Windows Server 2022 - Domain Controller
    - ACIDM01 - Windows Server 2022 - Domain Member Server
    - ACIWIN11 - Windows 11 - Domain Member Workstation

## Key Accomplishments

  1.  Security Monitoring and Log Management with Splunk

   - Installed and configured Splunk Enterprise for centralized log collection and analysis.
   - Deployed and configured Splunk Universal Forwarder on a Windows Server.
   - Configured forwarding and receiving ports to enable secure log transmission.
   - Collected and monitored Windows Event Logs, including Application, Security, and System logs.
   - Established a centralized logging solution to improve visibility into network activity and support security investigations.

  2. Data Protection with BitLocker Encryption

   - Installed the BitLocker Drive Encryption feature on Windows Server 2022.
   - Configured full-disk encryption on a local server volume.
   - Created and secured a BitLocker recovery key.
   - Validated successful encryption to protect sensitive data at rest and strengthen compliance with security best practices.

  3. Identity and Access Management with Multi-Factor Authentication

   - Created and managed Active Directory user accounts.
   - Implemented multi-factor authentication controls by requiring smart card authentication for interactive logon.
   - Tested and verified MFA enforcement to demonstrate protection against unauthorized account access.


## Summary

  Implemented enterprise security controls within a Windows domain environment by deploying Splunk Enterprise for centralized log management, configuring BitLocker encryption to protect sensitive data, and enabling multi-factor authentication through Active Directory. Demonstrated practical experience in SIEM deployment, security monitoring, data protection, and identity management aligned with CompTIA CySA+ objectives. 
